Commentary of Ibn Sa'di (Taysir al-Karim al-Rahman) on surah 47, verse 10–11:

{10} That is: Will not these deniers of the Messenger (ﷺ) travel through the land, {and see what was the end of those before them}? For they will find that their end is nothing but the worst of ends. Wherever they turn, right or left, they find that those around them have perished and been destroyed, uprooted by denial and disbelief, extinguished. God destroyed their wealth and their homes against them, indeed destroyed their deeds and their scheming. For the disbelievers in every time and place there are similar dire consequences and reprehensible punishments. As for the believers, God delivers them from the torment and bestows upon them abundant reward.

{11} {That is because God is the Protector (mawla) of those who believed}: so He takes them under His mercy, brings them out from the darknesses into the light, and takes charge of their recompense and their victory. {And that the disbelievers}: in God, the Exalted; in that they have cut themselves off from God's guardianship and shut off His mercy from themselves {have no protector}: who would guide them to the paths of peace, or deliver them from the punishment and retribution of God. Rather, their protectors are the taghut (false deities/tyrants), who bring them out from the light into the darknesses. {Those are the companions of the Fire; therein they will abide forever.}

